Subject: [PATCH] i386/acpi: omit fw_cfg discovery node from DSDT

Based on QEMU v10.2.4. The underlying fw_cfg I/O/DMA interface remains
accessible and its signatures are unchanged. Firmware still uses it.

--- a/hw/i386/acpi-build.c
+++ b/hw/i386/acpi-build.c
@@ -1183,12 +1183,7 @@
     aml_append(scope, aml_name_decl("_S5", pkg));
     aml_append(dsdt, scope);
 
-    /* create fw_cfg node, unconditionally */
-    {
-        scope = aml_scope("\\_SB.PCI0");
-        fw_cfg_add_acpi_dsdt(scope, x86ms->fw_cfg);
-        aml_append(dsdt, scope);
-    }
+    /* Keep fw_cfg for firmware, but omit its guest ACPI discovery node. */
 
     sb_scope = aml_scope("\\_SB");
     {
